# `-d @-` would source the request body from stdin. The daemon
# re-parses argv with an empty stdin handle, so the popover and
# audit log would record a 0-byte body while `vet` execs the real
# pipe. Reject in the parser; agents must materialise to a temp
# file and use `-d @file` instead. Sister to `upload_stdin.argv`
# (which closes the same gap for `-T -`). ThreatModel T9 close.
-d
@-
https://example.test/post
